date-released: "2026-05-22"
version: "1.0.3"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for the first pre-registered phenome-wide
  Mendelian randomization study of amyloid-PET cortical deposition against
  1,574 FinnGen R12 disease endpoints (N=500,348). The conservative
  wide-APOE-excluded instrument panel localises the AD causal signal to
  the chr1q32.2 CR1 region; the colocalisation replicates cleanly across
  cohort configurations (coloc.abf PP.H4 = 0.983 multi-ethnic primary,
  0.977 NHW EUR-only sub-meta), and per-gene SuSiE fine-mapping on
  full-pairs Brain_Cortex eQTL data (fetched byte-range from the EBI eQTL
  Catalogue) identifies CR1 as the most plausible mediating transcript
  over CR1L (no Brain_Cortex eQTL) and CD46 (credible set 238 kb from
  the amyloid signal). A pre-registered negative-control diagnostic is
  engaged as a tissue-of-action divergence. A post-hoc ADNI tau-PET
  polygenic-score cascade biological-validation arm (n=218 EUR with
  Berkeley flortaucipir tau-PET and Omni2.5M genotypes; OSF Amendment 5
  with model specification frozen pre-results) confirms the pre-registered
  amyloid PGS predicts meta-temporal tau-PET SUVR (beta=0.081, p=2.98e-5),
  persisting in APOE-e4 non-carriers (beta=0.044, p=4.5e-3, n=146) and
  supporting the wide-APOE-excluded CR1 localisation independently of the
  FinnGen MR. The deposit includes the locked 41-section pre-registration
  with 5 publicly-versioned amendments (4 pre-results + Amendment 5
  post-hoc with model frozen pre-results), the analytical pipeline (R +
  Python + bash; 20 R scripts including R/17 per-gene SuSiE decomposition,
  R/19 formal coloc.susie attempt with kriging diagnostic, R/19b
  cross-cohort coloc.abf cross-check, and R/20 ADNI tau-PET PGS cascade
  with primary + six pre-specified sensitivity analyses), the per-panel
  instrument lists, the Amyloid-PET Causal Atlas (7,870 rows x 46 cols)
  as parquet + TSV + interactive HTML browser, per-stage MR result
  parquets, ADNI cascade group-level summary TSVs (no individual-level
  ADNI data per the Data Use Agreement), manuscript figures (including
  the chr1q32.2 regional plot), and supplementary tables S1 (per-panel
  SNP inventory), S2 (per-gene SuSiE credible-set membership), and S3
  (ADNI cascade arm cohort details + full results). Code is licensed
  MIT; derived data products are licensed CC-BY 4.0 — see LICENSE file
  for full dual-licence terms. Upstream summary-level GWAS data,
  individual-level ADNI data, and reference panels are not redistributed;
  canonical sources and SHA256 hashes are documented for re-download.
